# {{ title }}

Directives are YAMD's only extension mechanism. There are three forms:

- Containers wrap blocks: `:::name {attrs}` … `:::`
- Leaves are one line: `::name[label]{attrs}`
- Inline directives sit in text: `:name[content]{attrs}`

::toc{depth=2}

## Callouts

:::note
A note adds helpful context.
:::

:::tip
Tips suggest a better way to do something.
:::

:::warning {title="Back up first"}
Warnings point out risks. This one has a custom title.
:::

:::danger
Danger callouts are for data loss or security problems.
:::

Callouts can hold any blocks:

:::tip {title="Keyboard shortcuts"}
| Action        | Shortcut          |
| ------------- | ----------------- |
| Open preview  | :kbd[Cmd+K V]     |
| Bold          | :kbd[Cmd+B]       |

- Shortcuts only apply in `.yamd` files.
:::

